                <pb facs="0123" n="31" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg31"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 7.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Legation to Hobbs &amp; Gifford.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-01-17"><hi rendition="#italic">January 17,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: I have the pleasure of informing you
                    that, upon the intervention of this legation the Government of Austria-Hungary
                    has recognized the American citizenship of your client, Mr. Erminio Demartini,
                    and has ordered his name to be stricken from the list of deserters from the
                    Austro-Hungarian army at Trieste.</p>
                <p>Mr. Demartini’s case has been duly reported by me to the Department of State at
                    Washington.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charlemagne
                    Tower.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
